# ─── Real data. Never committed. ───────────────────────────────────
# Only *.example.yml ships. Everything else in inputs/ is yours.
inputs/*
!inputs/*.example.yml
!inputs/README.md

# Generated reports. The folder ships; its contents never do.
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep

# Your statements, policies and returns. The folder and its README ship;
# nothing you put in it ever does. Note this ignores every extension, not a
# list of them -- a list is a promise to remember the next format.
documents/*
!documents/README.md

# A personal deny-list of your own name/address/policy numbers, for
# local secret scanning. MUST stay local — committing it would publish
# exactly the strings it exists to protect.
.gitleaks.local.toml

# A local list of your own values for scripts/privacy_audit.py. Same reason:
# committing it would publish exactly the strings it exists to protect.
.privacy-tokens.local

# ─── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ─── OS / editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Task briefs dropped into the repo root. They routinely quote real figures
# from the household they were written about -- that is what makes them
# useful -- and this is a public repository.
/*-prompt.md
/*-brief.md
